## Slice 1 — Transport diet: pose quantization + permessage-deflate

Cheapest win, zero behavioral risk, lands first so later slices are measured on the new baseline.

**Files:** `lib/net/codec.ts`, `server/room.ts`, `server/index.ts`, `lib/net/NetworkSession.ts`, `lib/net/protocol.test.ts` (or new `codec.test.ts`), `server/room.test.ts`, docs.

**Quantization helpers — in `codec.ts`** (encoding concern, imported by both ends; protocol.ts stays shapes-only):

```ts
/** 2-decimal position quantizer (1 cm) — wire-size only, no shape change. */
export const qPos = (v: number): number => Math.round(v * 100) / 100;
/** 3-decimal angle/velocity quantizer (~0.06°). */
export const qAng = (v: number): number => Math.round(v * 1000) / 1000;
```

Apply at serialization sites only (shadows/deadbands keep full precision):
- `server/room.ts`: `collectPlayerPoses` (x/y/z→qPos, yaw/pitch→qAng), `collectMobPoses`, `collectVehiclePoses`, `collectProjectilePoses` (velocity via qAng is fine at 3dp — orientation-only on the client), `rosterEntry`, and the mounted `x/y/z` in `buildSelfDelta`.
- `lib/net/NetworkSession.ts`: the 20 Hz pose sender in `afterFrame` and the `sendCmd` eye pose.

No protocol bump: identical field names/types, just shorter number literals. Sanity margins: 0.005 blocks ≪ the `applyRemotePose` clamps (+0.5 slack) and ≪ `MOB_DEADBAND_SQ`.

**permessage-deflate — `server/index.ts`**, inside the `websocket: {...}` config:

```ts
websocket: {
  // JSON tick frames are ~1–4 KB of highly repetitive keys; deflate gets 3–5×.
  perMessageDeflate: { compress: "16KB", decompress: true },
  open(ws) { ... },
```

Browsers negotiate `permessage-deflate` automatically when offered — no client change. Bun's own WebSocket client (used by `scripts/loadSim.ts` / `netProbe.ts`) offers it by default too (`bun-types/bun.d.ts:4264-4277`), so loadSim exercises the compression path realistically.

Risk assessment (shared-cpu-2x, 8 players × 3 rooms = 24 sockets @20 Hz): ~480 deflates/s of ~1–2 KB frames with 16 KB dedicated windows ≈ tens of µs each — well under 5% of one core; window memory ≈ 24 × ~50 KB ≈ 1.2 MB, trivial against the 512 MB VM. Verify with loadSim `slowestTickMs` before/after (see Slice 7). Fallback knob if CPU shows up: `{ compress: "8KB", decompress: false }`.

**Measurement caveat to document:** `Room.bytesOut` counts **pre-compression** `encoded.length`, so `/rooms` `kbOutPerSec` shows the quantization win but not the deflate win. Deflate savings are verified in Chrome DevTools (WS frame sizes + `Sec-WebSocket-Extensions` response header) and Fly egress metrics — say so in tuning.md.

**Tests:**
- `codec`: `qPos/qAng` round-trip through `JSON.stringify` at ≤6/7 chars for typical coords; negative/zero/±π cases.
- `room.test.ts`: new assertion in an existing pose-flow test — broadcast `pp`/`mp` values have ≤2/3 decimals (e.g. `Number.isInteger(pose.x * 100)`). Check existing tests that assert exact float positions (e.g. vehicle/arrow test around line 180) — update expectations to quantized values.
- `server.e2e-smoke.test.ts`: confirm handshake still passes with deflate enabled (Bun client negotiates it).

